STORES — `summarizer@2.1.0` carries no store, so nothing under it is a legal `seed_rows` target (`seed_target_not_a_store`).
PARAMS — `summarizer@2.1.0` is 3 cells, so `override_params` is KEYED BY CELL PATH ("" is the template root): "": contract{accepts, emits}, graph{edges}, ports; prep: external_timeout_ms, phaseout_chars, recent_turns, round_lines, runner, script_inline, tool_chars; writer: api_key, base_url, max_tokens, model, provider, system_order, temperature. A path or a key that list does not name is refused with `schema` and none of the manifest is applied. A `{…}` suffix is the key shape of the value this template SHIPS, not a required set.

